{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"While it's not required to know the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/history"},{"type":"text","value":" API itself to use TanStack Router, it's a good idea to understand how it works. Under the hood, TanStack Router requires and uses a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"history"},{"type":"text","value":" abstraction to manage the routing history."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If you don't create a history instance, a browser-oriented instance of this API is created for you when the router is initialized. If you need a special history API type, You can use the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/history"},{"type":"text","value":" package to create your own:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createBrowserHistory"},{"type":"text","value":": The default history type."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createHashHistory"},{"type":"text","value":": A history type that uses a hash to track history."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createMemoryHistory"},{"type":"text","value":": A history type that keeps the history in memory."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createServerHistory"},{"type":"text","value":": A history type with a fixed request URL and no-op navigation, used by the SSR request handlers."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Once you have a history instance, you can pass it to the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Router"},{"type":"text","value":" constructor:"}]},{"type":"component","name":"framework","attributes":{},"children":[{"type":"component","name":"framework-panel","tagName":"md-framework-panel","attributes":{},"properties":{"data-framework":"react"},"children":[{"type":"code","value":"import { createMemoryHistory, createRouter } from '@tanstack/react-router'\n\nconst memoryHistory = createMemoryHistory({\n  initialEntries: ['/'], // Pass your initial url\n})\n\nconst router = createRouter({ routeTree, history: memoryHistory })","lang":"ts"}]},{"type":"component","name":"framework-panel","tagName":"md-framework-panel","attributes":{},"properties":{"data-framework":"solid"},"children":[{"type":"code","value":"import { createMemoryHistory, createRouter } from '@tanstack/solid-router'\n\nconst memoryHistory = createMemoryHistory({\n  initialEntries: ['/'], // Pass your initial url\n})\n\nconst router = createRouter({ routeTree, history: memoryHistory })","lang":"ts"}]}],"properties":{"data-available-frameworks":"[\"react\",\"solid\"]","data-framework-meta":"{\"codeBlocksByFramework\":{\"react\":[{\"title\":\"\",\"code\":\"import { createMemoryHistory, createRouter } from '@tanstack/react-router'\\n\\nconst memoryHistory = createMemoryHistory({\\n  initialEntries: ['/'], // Pass your initial url\\n})\\n\\nconst router = createRouter({ routeTree, history: memoryHistory })\",\"language\":\"ts\"}],\"solid\":[{\"title\":\"\",\"code\":\"import { createMemoryHistory, createRouter } from '@tanstack/solid-router'\\n\\nconst memoryHistory = createMemoryHistory({\\n  initialEntries: ['/'], // Pass your initial url\\n})\\n\\nconst router = createRouter({ routeTree, history: memoryHistory })\",\"language\":\"ts\"}]}}"}},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"browser-routing","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Browser Routing"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createBrowserHistory"},{"type":"text","value":" is the default history type. It uses the browser's history API to manage the browser history."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"hash-routing","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Hash Routing"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Hash routing can be helpful if your server doesn't support rewrites to index.html for HTTP requests (among other environments that don't have a server)."}]},{"type":"component","name":"framework","attributes":{},"children":[{"type":"component","name":"framework-panel","tagName":"md-framework-panel","attributes":{},"properties":{"data-framework":"react"},"children":[{"type":"code","value":"import { createHashHistory, createRouter } from '@tanstack/react-router'\n\nconst hashHistory = createHashHistory()\n\nconst router = createRouter({ routeTree, history: hashHistory })","lang":"ts"}]},{"type":"component","name":"framework-panel","tagName":"md-framework-panel","attributes":{},"properties":{"data-framework":"solid"},"children":[{"type":"code","value":"import { createHashHistory, createRouter } from '@tanstack/solid-router'\n\nconst hashHistory = createHashHistory()\n\nconst router = createRouter({ routeTree, history: hashHistory })","lang":"ts"}]}],"properties":{"data-available-frameworks":"[\"react\",\"solid\"]","data-framework-meta":"{\"codeBlocksByFramework\":{\"react\":[{\"title\":\"\",\"code\":\"import { createHashHistory, createRouter } from '@tanstack/react-router'\\n\\nconst hashHistory = createHashHistory()\\n\\nconst router = createRouter({ routeTree, history: hashHistory })\",\"language\":\"ts\"}],\"solid\":[{\"title\":\"\",\"code\":\"import { createHashHistory, createRouter } from '@tanstack/solid-router'\\n\\nconst hashHistory = createHashHistory()\\n\\nconst router = createRouter({ routeTree, history: hashHistory })\",\"language\":\"ts\"}]}}"}},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"memory-routing","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Memory Routing"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Memory routing is useful in environments that are not a browser or when you do not want components to interact with the URL."}]},{"type":"component","name":"framework","attributes":{},"children":[{"type":"component","name":"framework-panel","tagName":"md-framework-panel","attributes":{},"properties":{"data-framework":"react"},"children":[{"type":"code","value":"import { createMemoryHistory, createRouter } from '@tanstack/react-router'\n\nconst memoryHistory = createMemoryHistory({\n  initialEntries: ['/'], // Pass your initial url\n})\n\nconst router = createRouter({ routeTree, history: memoryHistory })","lang":"ts"}]},{"type":"component","name":"framework-panel","tagName":"md-framework-panel","attributes":{},"properties":{"data-framework":"solid"},"children":[{"type":"code","value":"import { createMemoryHistory, createRouter } from '@tanstack/solid-router'\n\nconst memoryHistory = createMemoryHistory({\n  initialEntries: ['/'], // Pass your initial url\n})\n\nconst router = createRouter({ routeTree, history: memoryHistory })","lang":"ts"}]}],"properties":{"data-available-frameworks":"[\"react\",\"solid\"]","data-framework-meta":"{\"codeBlocksByFramework\":{\"react\":[{\"title\":\"\",\"code\":\"import { createMemoryHistory, createRouter } from '@tanstack/react-router'\\n\\nconst memoryHistory = createMemoryHistory({\\n  initialEntries: ['/'], // Pass your initial url\\n})\\n\\nconst router = createRouter({ routeTree, history: memoryHistory })\",\"language\":\"ts\"}],\"solid\":[{\"title\":\"\",\"code\":\"import { createMemoryHistory, createRouter } from '@tanstack/solid-router'\\n\\nconst memoryHistory = createMemoryHistory({\\n  initialEntries: ['/'], // Pass your initial url\\n})\\n\\nconst router = createRouter({ routeTree, history: memoryHistory })\",\"language\":\"ts\"}]}}"}},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Refer to the "},{"type":"link","href":"./ssr.md#automatic-server-history","children":[{"type":"text","value":"SSR Guide"}]},{"type":"text","value":" for usage on the server for server-side rendering."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"browser-routing","text":"Browser Routing","level":2},{"id":"hash-routing","text":"Hash Routing","level":2},{"id":"memory-routing","text":"Memory Routing","level":2}]},"frameworks":["react","solid"],"downloadMarkdown":"\nWhile it's not required to know the `@tanstack/history` API itself to use TanStack Router, it's a good idea to understand how it works. Under the hood, TanStack Router requires and uses a `history` abstraction to manage the routing history.\n\nIf you don't create a history instance, a browser-oriented instance of this API is created for you when the router is initialized. If you need a special history API type, You can use the `@tanstack/history` package to create your own:\n\n- `createBrowserHistory`: The default history type.\n- `createHashHistory`: A history type that uses a hash to track history.\n- `createMemoryHistory`: A history type that keeps the history in memory.\n- `createServerHistory`: A history type with a fixed request URL and no-op navigation, used by the SSR request handlers.\n\nOnce you have a history instance, you can pass it to the `Router` constructor:\n\n<!-- ::start:framework -->\n\n# React\n\n```ts\nimport { createMemoryHistory, createRouter } from '@tanstack/react-router'\n\nconst memoryHistory = createMemoryHistory({\n  initialEntries: ['/'], // Pass your initial url\n})\n\nconst router = createRouter({ routeTree, history: memoryHistory })\n```\n\n# Solid\n\n```ts\nimport { createMemoryHistory, createRouter } from '@tanstack/solid-router'\n\nconst memoryHistory = createMemoryHistory({\n  initialEntries: ['/'], // Pass your initial url\n})\n\nconst router = createRouter({ routeTree, history: memoryHistory })\n```\n\n<!-- ::end:framework -->\n\n## Browser Routing\n\nThe `createBrowserHistory` is the default history type. It uses the browser's history API to manage the browser history.\n\n## Hash Routing\n\nHash routing can be helpful if your server doesn't support rewrites to index.html for HTTP requests (among other environments that don't have a server).\n\n<!-- ::start:framework -->\n\n# React\n\n```ts\nimport { createHashHistory, createRouter } from '@tanstack/react-router'\n\nconst hashHistory = createHashHistory()\n\nconst router = createRouter({ routeTree, history: hashHistory })\n```\n\n# Solid\n\n```ts\nimport { createHashHistory, createRouter } from '@tanstack/solid-router'\n\nconst hashHistory = createHashHistory()\n\nconst router = createRouter({ routeTree, history: hashHistory })\n```\n\n<!-- ::end:framework -->\n\n## Memory Routing\n\nMemory routing is useful in environments that are not a browser or when you do not want components to interact with the URL.\n\n<!-- ::start:framework -->\n\n# React\n\n```ts\nimport { createMemoryHistory, createRouter } from '@tanstack/react-router'\n\nconst memoryHistory = createMemoryHistory({\n  initialEntries: ['/'], // Pass your initial url\n})\n\nconst router = createRouter({ routeTree, history: memoryHistory })\n```\n\n# Solid\n\n```ts\nimport { createMemoryHistory, createRouter } from '@tanstack/solid-router'\n\nconst memoryHistory = createMemoryHistory({\n  initialEntries: ['/'], // Pass your initial url\n})\n\nconst router = createRouter({ routeTree, history: memoryHistory })\n```\n\n<!-- ::end:framework -->\n\nRefer to the [SSR Guide](./ssr.md#automatic-server-history) for usage on the server for server-side rendering.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: History Types\n---\n\nWhile it's not required to know the `@tanstack/history` API itself to use TanStack Router, it's a good idea to understand how it works. Under the hood, TanStack Router requires and uses a `history` abstraction to manage the routing history.\n\nIf you don't create a history instance, a browser-oriented instance of this API is created for you when the router is initialized. If you need a special history API type, You can use the `@tanstack/history` package to create your own:\n\n- `createBrowserHistory`: The default history type.\n- `createHashHistory`: A history type that uses a hash to track history.\n- `createMemoryHistory`: A history type that keeps the history in memory.\n- `createServerHistory`: A history type with a fixed request URL and no-op navigation, used by the SSR request handlers.\n\nOnce you have a history instance, you can pass it to the `Router` constructor:\n\n<!-- ::start:framework -->\n\n# React\n\n```ts\nimport { createMemoryHistory, createRouter } from '@tanstack/react-router'\n\nconst memoryHistory = createMemoryHistory({\n  initialEntries: ['/'], // Pass your initial url\n})\n\nconst router = createRouter({ routeTree, history: memoryHistory })\n```\n\n# Solid\n\n```ts\nimport { createMemoryHistory, createRouter } from '@tanstack/solid-router'\n\nconst memoryHistory = createMemoryHistory({\n  initialEntries: ['/'], // Pass your initial url\n})\n\nconst router = createRouter({ routeTree, history: memoryHistory })\n```\n\n<!-- ::end:framework -->\n\n## Browser Routing\n\nThe `createBrowserHistory` is the default history type. It uses the browser's history API to manage the browser history.\n\n## Hash Routing\n\nHash routing can be helpful if your server doesn't support rewrites to index.html for HTTP requests (among other environments that don't have a server).\n\n<!-- ::start:framework -->\n\n# React\n\n```ts\nimport { createHashHistory, createRouter } from '@tanstack/react-router'\n\nconst hashHistory = createHashHistory()\n\nconst router = createRouter({ routeTree, history: hashHistory })\n```\n\n# Solid\n\n```ts\nimport { createHashHistory, createRouter } from '@tanstack/solid-router'\n\nconst hashHistory = createHashHistory()\n\nconst router = createRouter({ routeTree, history: hashHistory })\n```\n\n<!-- ::end:framework -->\n\n## Memory Routing\n\nMemory routing is useful in environments that are not a browser or when you do not want components to interact with the URL.\n\n<!-- ::start:framework -->\n\n# React\n\n```ts\nimport { createMemoryHistory, createRouter } from '@tanstack/react-router'\n\nconst memoryHistory = createMemoryHistory({\n  initialEntries: ['/'], // Pass your initial url\n})\n\nconst router = createRouter({ routeTree, history: memoryHistory })\n```\n\n# Solid\n\n```ts\nimport { createMemoryHistory, createRouter } from '@tanstack/solid-router'\n\nconst memoryHistory = createMemoryHistory({\n  initialEntries: ['/'], // Pass your initial url\n})\n\nconst router = createRouter({ routeTree, history: memoryHistory })\n```\n\n<!-- ::end:framework -->\n\nRefer to the [SSR Guide](./ssr.md#automatic-server-history) for usage on the server for server-side rendering.\n"}
